{
  "title": "🧩 Probability Problem-Solving — Putting It All Together",
  "hook": "Now that you know the formulas, let's tackle the REAL challenge — word problems! From coins to cards to numbered balls, let's develop a systematic approach.",
  "explanation": "<div style=\"margin:12px 0\"><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\"><div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#E65100;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">1</div><div><strong>Read carefully — what's the experiment?</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\">Coin toss? Die roll? Drawing a card? Picking a ball?</span></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\"><div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#E65100;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">2</div><div><strong>List the sample space (or at least count outcomes)</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\"></span></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\"><div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#E65100;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">3</div><div><strong>Identify the event — what are 'favourable' outcomes?</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\"></span></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\"><div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#E65100;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">4</div><div><strong>Count favourable outcomes</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\">Use listing, combination, or logic</span></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\"><div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#E65100;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">5</div><div><strong>Apply P(E) = favourable / total</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\"></span></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\"><div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#E65100;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">6</div><div><strong>Check: is your answer between 0 and 1?</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\">Sanity check!</span></div></div></div><div style=\"background:#E3F2FD;border-left:4px solid #1565C0;border-radius:8px;padding:10px 14px;margin:10px 0;font-size:0.88rem\">ℹ️ <strong>Tip:</strong> <b>Common traps:</b><br>• Two dice: (3,4) and (4,3) are DIFFERENT outcomes (total 36, not 21).<br>• Cards: suit matters! King of Hearts ≠ King of Spades.<br>• 'At least one' → use complement method: 1 − P(none).</div><table style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin:12px 0;font-size:0.88rem\"><tr><th style=\"background:#E3F2FD;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #BBDEFB;text-align:left;font-weight:700\">Problem Type</th><th style=\"background:#E3F2FD;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #BBDEFB;text-align:left;font-weight:700\">Strategy</th></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">'At least one'</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">Use complement: 1 − P(none)</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">'Both' or 'all'</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">Multiply individual probabilities (if independent)</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">'Or' (either/or)</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">Add: P(A) + P(B) − P(A and B)</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">With replacement</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">Probabilities stay same each draw</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">Without replacement</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">Probabilities change after each draw</td></tr></table>",
  "worked_example": "<b>Example:</b> Numbers 1-20 are written on tickets and put in a box. One ticket is drawn at random. Find: (a) P(multiple of 3 or 5), (b) P(multiple of 3 and 5).<br><br><div style=\"margin:12px 0\"><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\"><div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#4A90D9;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">1</div><div><strong>Multiples of 3: {3,6,9,12,15,18} → 6 numbers</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\"></span></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\"><div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#4A90D9;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">2</div><div><strong>Multiples of 5: {5,10,15,20} → 4 numbers</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\"></span></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\"><div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#4A90D9;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">3</div><div><strong>Multiples of both 3 and 5 (i.e., 15): {15} → 1 number</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\"></span></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\"><div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#4A90D9;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">4</div><div><strong>P(3 or 5) = (6+4−1)/20 = 9/20</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\">Subtract 15 to avoid double counting</span></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\"><div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#4A90D9;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">5</div><div><strong>P(3 and 5) = 1/20</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\">Only 15</span></div></div></div>",
